WEBVTT

00:05.420 --> 00:07.750
Well, look at you.

00:15.320 --> 00:18.920
In the month since you were born, you've 
defeated the master of the northern woods,

00:18.920 --> 00:21.700
and evolved into a ogre...

00:22.700 --> 00:26.260
<i>After the conversation finally wound down...</i>

00:27.130 --> 00:30.760
<i>Why are they following me? 
Am I a mother duck now?</i>

00:30.760 --> 00:34.510
<i>Well, personally, I want new clothes 
before anything else.</i>

00:34.510 --> 00:35.880
No—!

00:35.880 --> 00:37.020
<i>Yeah, that's fair.</i>

00:37.780 --> 00:40.990
<i>Their reaction had wounded 
me a little on the inside,</i>

00:40.990 --> 00:44.520
<i>but they seem to understand 
who I am, so I guess it's fine.</i>

00:44.920 --> 00:46.980
<i>For now, I'll ignore the fact</i>

00:47.390 --> 00:51.030
<i>that Gobmi keeps pinching my leg...</i>

02:26.520 --> 02:30.170
Wow, you've really gotten 
a lot of use out of it.

02:30.170 --> 02:32.160
Guess I'd better do something.

02:33.080 --> 02:37.650
By the way, I used spirit stone to make 
a knife earlier! You should check it out.

02:37.650 --> 02:39.920
That does sound interesting!

02:40.290 --> 02:41.520
I appreciate it.

02:43.730 --> 02:47.270
<i>I love it when a girl looks tickled like this.</i>

02:49.430 --> 02:52.900
<i>Why? Why are they pinching harder now?</i>

02:53.550 --> 02:57.350
It's actually kind of hard 
with just the two of us.

02:57.350 --> 03:01.290
So some extra hands would be a big help.

03:01.290 --> 03:05.180
Maybe three of the lady goblins 
from the rear support team...

03:05.180 --> 03:06.580
Perfect!

03:05.560 --> 03:07.290
That'd be a huge help!

03:07.880 --> 03:11.150
<i>I have to say, goblins 
are their bitter enemies,</i>

03:11.150 --> 03:13.070
<i>but they've made themselves 
at home pretty quickly...</i>

03:13.070 --> 03:16.800
<i>That's an impressive bit of 
resilience and adaptablity.</i>

03:17.070 --> 03:20.070
You two seem like you'll make great wives.

03:20.070 --> 03:21.810
How about it? Interested?

03:21.810 --> 03:23.990
Oh, come on. You're such a flatterer.

03:23.990 --> 03:27.310
<i>The way they smile when 
they don't mind it is also cute!</i>

03:24.750 --> 03:26.500
We might take you seriously, y'know.

03:28.090 --> 03:30.290
<i>But this is going a little too far.</i>

03:31.160 --> 03:34.690
<i>The alchemist had returned 
to her potion crafting.</i>

03:34.690 --> 03:35.690
How can I help you?

03:36.200 --> 03:38.280
Hey, isn't this...

03:38.280 --> 03:39.970
I'm impressed you noticed.

03:39.970 --> 03:42.330
It's poison, yes.

03:42.330 --> 03:44.200
For what, exactly?

03:46.310 --> 03:48.210
It was for protection.

03:49.230 --> 03:55.130
But now that I know that there are 
trustworthy goblins like you...

03:55.130 --> 03:57.840
I don't intend to 
use it on food anymore.

03:58.190 --> 04:00.500
It's the bare minimum of preparation.

04:01.030 --> 04:05.350
I have to say, you've become so impressive, 
I wasn't sure what to do.

04:07.480 --> 04:09.840
Well, it's not like I can help it, can I?

04:09.840 --> 04:12.250
Come on, stop.

04:14.430 --> 04:17.610
<i>The bashful smile of a cool beauty 
is a sight to behold!</i>

04:20.130 --> 04:23.240
<i>I can feel the icy chill 
of a glare with killer intent!</i>

04:24.740 --> 04:30.130
<i>I ended up having to spend a lot longer 
cheering the girls up than I expected,</i>

04:30.130 --> 04:32.750
<i>which made me more
mentally than physically tired...</i>

04:33.250 --> 04:35.750
<b>Day 36</b>

04:33.730 --> 04:39.260
<i>And the next day, I wasn't able to 
do my usual afternoon sparring.</i>

04:44.000 --> 04:47.890
<i>Normal goblins are on the verge of death 
if I hit them even gently...</i>

04:47.890 --> 04:52.020
<i>And Gobkichi's armor almost broke,
 so we had to call it off.</i>

04:52.020 --> 04:55.920
Sorry about that. Almost got you killed.

04:58.030 --> 05:00.120
Gobkichi, what's wrong?

05:00.120 --> 05:03.030
No... it's nothing. I'm gonna go hunt.

05:05.610 --> 05:08.450
<i>Sure doesn't look like it's nothing.</i>

05:10.490 --> 05:11.540
<i>Afterwards...</i>

05:11.540 --> 05:14.340
I really think we have a lot in common!

05:12.190 --> 05:15.570
<i>Gobmi and Hobsato went out hunting together.</i>

05:14.340 --> 05:16.290
I get what you mean!

05:16.300 --> 05:20.300
<i>Gobe mined for spirit stone, 
which has become a hobby.</i>

05:16.300 --> 05:20.300
Hell yeah! Let's get it!

05:20.670 --> 05:23.800
<i>While the short-haired redhead 
focused on her personal training.</i>

05:24.430 --> 05:26.550
As for me...

05:27.270 --> 05:31.800
I see that having your left arm eaten 
hasn't slowed you down any.

05:31.800 --> 05:33.860
You'd be surprised what you can get used to.

05:33.860 --> 05:36.570
<i>It's actually thanks to a slime I ate before.</i>

05:37.070 --> 05:40.680
I'm curious... Do you think 
Gobkichi will be okay?

05:41.230 --> 05:44.570
That'll probably depend 
on how he reacts, really.

05:44.570 --> 05:47.100
I guess that's true. By the way...

05:47.100 --> 05:49.440
Could you maybe give me that book back now?

05:50.840 --> 05:53.920
Come on, the silent treatment?! 
I haven't finished reading it yet!

05:53.920 --> 05:58.090
Are you listening, Hobsei?! Miss Hobsei?!

05:54.640 --> 05:57.040
He's having a good time.

05:59.010 --> 06:03.090
<i>I was able to have a peaceful day 
for the first time in a while.</i>

06:03.590 --> 06:06.090
<b>Day 37</b>

06:06.460 --> 06:11.110
<i>After morning training was over, 
and I was casually enjoying lunch...</i>

06:11.650 --> 06:13.600
We've got real trouble, Gobrou!

06:13.600 --> 06:17.620
I dunno what to do! 
You've gotta help me out here!

06:17.930 --> 06:21.140
<i>She was carrying a carbuncle 
that was covered in blood.</i>

06:21.140 --> 06:23.790
<i>The first thing was to try was healing her.</i>

06:24.610 --> 06:27.770
I-I was just digging through 
some walls, and she fell out!

06:27.770 --> 06:29.410
She's lost a lot of blood.

06:29.730 --> 06:32.620
I'm gonna get something from 
the alchemist to help her.

06:38.370 --> 06:39.610
She's awake.

06:39.610 --> 06:42.880
Where am I? And who are you?

06:43.390 --> 06:47.390
<i>After explaining the situation, 
the carbuncle opened up.</i>

06:47.390 --> 06:52.070
Thank you for healing me despite 
being complete strangers.

06:52.070 --> 06:54.440
My name is Returner.

06:54.440 --> 06:57.650
I was actually attacked by
 some humans not long ago.

06:59.240 --> 07:03.210
<i>It seems the gem on a carbuncle's 
forehead is worth a lot of money,</i>

07:03.210 --> 07:06.240
<i>going for as much as a billion gold.</i>

07:06.910 --> 07:09.150
<i>This smells like trouble.</i>

07:09.150 --> 07:12.900
<i>That seems to be the reason 
human adventurers attacked her.</i>

07:12.900 --> 07:15.410
I realize how rude it is to ask this...

07:15.970 --> 07:19.520
Please, help me chase off these adventurers!

07:19.520 --> 07:21.920
I'm not long for this world.

07:24.940 --> 07:29.400
Please, lend me your strength! Please!

07:26.690 --> 07:30.510
<i>It turns out Returner is an artificial 
carbuncle created a long time ago</i>

07:30.510 --> 07:36.940
<i>by a legendary mage named Velvet, and 
the guardian of her master's old treasury.</i>

07:37.360 --> 07:39.240
<i>When she was attacked by those humans,</i>

07:39.240 --> 07:42.500
<i>the core that keeps her alive 
was damaged pretty badly,</i>

07:42.500 --> 07:44.940
<i>which means she won't live much longer.</i>

07:44.940 --> 07:50.180
<i>And that hidden treasury 
is apparently filled with</i>

07:50.180 --> 07:53.450
<i>all kinds of legendary items that 
Velvet spent his lifetime collecting.</i>

07:53.450 --> 07:56.210
My master disliked humans.

07:56.210 --> 08:00.650
He would rather leave his legacy to you all
than have it fall into their hands.

08:00.650 --> 08:03.480
I will hand over the entire contents 
of the treasury to you all.

08:04.690 --> 08:07.040
Whacha wanna do, Gobrou?

08:10.130 --> 08:11.970
Call the others.

08:12.930 --> 08:17.550
And there you have it. 
We're headed to this treasury today.

08:17.980 --> 08:22.050
Miss Smith, do you have the thing 
you mentioned the other day?

08:22.050 --> 08:25.180
O-Oh, the spirit stone knife, right?

08:25.180 --> 08:28.890
This should be a lot more intimidating 
than going around empty-handed,

08:28.890 --> 08:31.490
so I'm hoping it'll prove a good deterrent.

08:32.470 --> 08:37.000
I know, don't worry. 
I'm not looking to kill these humans.

08:37.000 --> 08:39.530
The job is to chase them off.

08:39.530 --> 08:41.630
I'll try to reason with them...

08:41.630 --> 08:44.880
But if that doesn't work, 
I'll have to do it the hard way.

08:44.880 --> 08:47.010
O-Okay. Be careful.

08:47.360 --> 08:51.450
<i>And so, we passed through the hole 
that Gobe accidentally opened up...</i>

08:51.450 --> 08:54.410
<i>and headed towards Velvet's hidden treasury.</i>

08:55.010 --> 08:57.530
Man, you really took down the whole wall.

08:57.530 --> 08:59.020
I was real shocked!

08:59.020 --> 09:03.860
<i>First, I asked Gobkichi and the others to 
hide so that I could try and negotiate.</i>

09:03.860 --> 09:07.030
<i>I looked for the adventurers 
on my own, but...</i>

09:09.590 --> 09:13.230
What the hell is this place? 
There's even a variant ogre down here.

09:13.230 --> 09:14.930
This is gonna be a pain.

09:14.930 --> 09:17.850
Between this and the skeletons, 
there's so much crap to deal with.

09:14.930 --> 09:18.900
<i>I'm actually a rare species, not a variant.</i>

09:17.850 --> 09:19.790
It's fine, let's just get rid of him.

09:19.790 --> 09:23.000
Yeah, we have to find that little one 
and take her treasure.

09:25.400 --> 09:26.630
H-he saw me coming?!

09:26.630 --> 09:29.420
An assassin's presence 
concealment doesn't work?!

09:29.420 --> 09:31.130
Listen up, boys!

09:31.490 --> 09:34.460
This is someone else's home, understand?

09:34.460 --> 09:37.480
Are you going around killing the inhabitants 
without even being invited in,

09:37.480 --> 09:40.630
on top of trying to rob the place?

09:41.060 --> 09:44.770
Sounds to me like a case of
 attempted murder and robbery.

09:44.770 --> 09:48.650
And to make things worse, you don't even 
seem to realize what you're doing is wrong.

09:49.160 --> 09:53.150
Dammit! Where does this ogre 
get off blabbing like a human?!

09:53.500 --> 09:55.590
You're lucky, though.

09:55.590 --> 09:58.660
I'm actually a pretty nice guy.

09:59.720 --> 10:00.660
Shut up!

10:01.010 --> 10:02.660
<i>Oh, well...</i>

10:06.460 --> 10:09.960
If you turn back now,
I'll let you leave. How about it?

10:10.920 --> 10:15.460
<i>I see. The three in the rear are packing 
some pretty high-quality magic items...</i>

10:15.740 --> 10:19.880
<i>But on the whole, their fighting is shoddy. 
There's something off about them.</i>

10:19.880 --> 10:22.850
<i>They've relied so much on boosting 
themselves with levels and job tweaks</i>

10:22.850 --> 10:25.350
<i>that they haven't put in the effort 
to work on their fundamentals.</i>

10:27.270 --> 10:30.780
<i>That would explain these simplistic attacks.</i>

10:33.110 --> 10:36.110
There! I blew his damn head off.

10:36.750 --> 10:38.260
Serves him right!

10:43.740 --> 10:47.770
<i>And now, my patience has run out.</i>

10:55.060 --> 10:56.090
No way!

10:56.090 --> 11:00.590
Th-That was a th-third-level magic spell!

11:03.550 --> 11:08.830
Sorry, but after that, 
even my patience has run out.

11:13.690 --> 11:14.820
Now...

11:15.260 --> 11:20.830
You're gonna regret not being reasonable.

11:25.530 --> 11:29.840
<i>After stripping the adventurers for 
everything they had, we split their belongings.</i>

11:30.080 --> 11:31.870
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Job: Assassin]</b>

11:30.090 --> 11:33.600
<i>Assassin. Crusader. Guardian.</i>

11:31.870 --> 11:33.170
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Job: Crusader]</b>

11:33.170 --> 11:34.330
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Job: Guardian]</b>

11:33.600 --> 11:37.380
<i>High Wizard. Priest. Enchanter.</i>

11:34.330 --> 11:35.340
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Job: High Wizard]</b>

11:35.340 --> 11:36.250
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Job: Priest]</b>

11:36.250 --> 11:37.460
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Job: Enchanter]</b>

11:37.460 --> 11:41.970
m 0 0 l 100 0 100 50 0 50

11:37.460 --> 11:41.970
<b>Six Magic Backpacks,
capable of storing up to 99
copies of 200 types of item
in their internal storage
dimension.</b>

11:37.920 --> 11:41.530
<i>They seemed to be pretty high level 
adventurers, as far as humans go.</i>

11:41.970 --> 11:44.970
<b>Hermit's Ring: [Status Concealment]
Magic ring that prevents wearer's
information from being assessed.</b>

11:41.970 --> 11:44.970
m 0 0 l 110 0 110 30 0 30

11:41.970 --> 11:47.330
<i>Their gear seemed to be 
high quality, so I ate all of it.</i>

11:48.230 --> 11:49.850
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Status Concealment]</b>

11:48.690 --> 11:51.770
<i>Status Concealment. Item Box.</i>

11:49.850 --> 11:51.770
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Item Box]</b>

11:52.020 --> 11:57.020
<i>I was pretty happy with the magic box that could contain 99 copies of 1200 different items,</i>

11:57.020 --> 11:58.500
<i>which, frankly, seems like overkill.</i>

11:58.790 --> 12:03.940
<i>Having delivered on our promise, we were 
led to the treasury in the deepest chamber.</i>

12:08.930 --> 12:11.990
Thank you all so much.

12:11.990 --> 12:14.290
I'm sure my master would be pleased.

12:14.300 --> 12:17.000
And this is Velvet?

12:17.000 --> 12:17.800
Yes.

12:17.800 --> 12:21.720
My master was very skilled in
 communicating with the spirits.

12:21.720 --> 12:26.810
That is why you'll be able to recover 
a wide variety of spirit stones here.

12:28.020 --> 12:30.230
He must've been quite the wizard.

12:30.230 --> 12:31.880
Oh, yes, very much so.

12:32.530 --> 12:34.310
But I'm afraid I'm out of time.

12:37.090 --> 12:40.120
Gobrou, please, be well.

12:46.900 --> 12:49.650
This is for the best, right?

12:50.000 --> 12:50.940
Yeah.

12:52.460 --> 12:54.710
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Golden Order]</b>

12:52.950 --> 12:54.710
<i>Golden Order.</i>

12:57.880 --> 12:59.270
You okay?

12:59.270 --> 13:01.210
Yeah, I'm fine.

13:01.930 --> 13:03.990
Thanks for worrying, Kichi.

13:07.650 --> 13:13.990
<i>After a moment of silence for Returner, 
we split up and collected everything of value.</i>

13:13.990 --> 13:17.240
<i>And man, that item box came in handy.</i>

13:17.240 --> 13:19.980
<i>Even with all of the treasures in it,
 there was still plenty of room left.</i>

13:24.620 --> 13:28.990
<i>I didn't like the idea of leaving 
the body, so I cremated it.</i>

13:46.980 --> 13:48.680
<i>I guess...</i>

13:48.680 --> 13:53.190
<i>I'll interpret this as him handing off 
some stuff he won't need anymore.</i>

13:48.930 --> 13:53.180
<b>Divine Legacy: [Legendary] Class
[Arm Blast] [Spell Blast]
[Self Evolution] [Attribute Echo]</b>

13:53.190 --> 13:55.160
What happened to your arm?!

13:55.160 --> 13:59.000
<i>It can rotate and transform at will, 
along with producing poison and string.</i>

13:59.260 --> 14:03.300
<i>And it works as well as a natural arm would.</i>

14:05.200 --> 14:08.450
<i>Then, having completed Returner's request...</i>

14:08.450 --> 14:10.200
Okay, everybody!

14:10.200 --> 14:11.880
We're gonna have a party!

14:11.880 --> 14:14.450
<i>Because there was some good 
stuff in our loot!</i>

14:15.080 --> 14:16.210
Booze!

14:16.210 --> 14:18.710
Cheers!

14:19.210 --> 14:22.340
<b>Day 38</b>

14:19.970 --> 14:22.340
<i>I'm assessing our collection 
with the blacksmith today.</i>

14:22.640 --> 14:26.840
<i>And like you'd expect from a legendary mage, 
most of it was pretty incredible.</i>

14:27.340 --> 14:30.470
<b>Day 39</b>

14:28.240 --> 14:30.470
Okay, everybody here?

14:31.210 --> 14:35.470
<i>I provided magic items 
to our 15 hobgoblins.</i>

14:36.340 --> 14:39.210
<i>I took the vermilion spear, Kaziklu Bey.</i>

14:39.210 --> 14:41.950
<i>Along with the magic bracelet, Solitary Fury.</i>

14:41.950 --> 14:46.960
<i>Add those to my silver arm, and 
I now have three legendary artifacts.</i>

14:48.130 --> 14:51.620
<i>Legendary is a rank for items,</i>

14:51.620 --> 14:55.000
<i>and valuable enough that entire 
countries will take action for them.</i>

14:55.350 --> 14:58.140
<i>In the afternoon, we gathered 
the ingredients for bear stew.</i>

14:59.000 --> 15:02.250
<i>Hunting was much easier with
 everyone's improved skills.</i>

15:03.040 --> 15:06.260
<i>And the bear stew was delicious! But...</i>

15:07.050 --> 15:12.350
<i>I did find it a little concerning that the short 
red-haired girl didn't do any fighting.</i>

15:13.260 --> 15:19.270
<b>Day 40</b>

15:13.650 --> 15:17.240
<i>Today, we're having a series of battles 
to determine the hobgoblins' ranks,</i>

15:17.240 --> 15:19.270
<i>with myself excluded.</i>

15:19.960 --> 15:23.030
<i>Everyone's leveled up nicely.</i>

15:23.390 --> 15:27.530
<i>Y'know, maybe we could form 
a mercenary company!</i>

15:28.030 --> 15:30.530
<b>Day 41</b>

15:29.430 --> 15:30.530
<i>Early that morning...</i>

15:30.800 --> 15:34.740
<i>I headed into the mountains on my own 
in pursuit of previously unseen prey.</i>

15:35.950 --> 15:37.910
<i>First was a golden spider.</i>

15:38.280 --> 15:40.550
<i>After prying off its 
expensive-looking carapace,</i>

15:40.550 --> 15:42.830
<i>I ate its meat, which was even 
better than the demon spider's!</i>

15:43.090 --> 15:45.000
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Gold String]</b>

15:43.090 --> 15:47.220
<i>Gold Thread. Golden Spider’s Shell.</i>

15:45.000 --> 15:47.220
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Golden Spider's Shell]</b>

15:48.290 --> 15:50.470
<i>I could become a fashion 
designer with this.</i>

15:51.110 --> 15:54.980
<i>A red deer, with antlers that look 
like they're made out of rose quartz.</i>

15:57.820 --> 16:00.980
<i>I think I'll need to eat another 
two or three to learn what I need.</i>

16:02.380 --> 16:06.910
<i>And as I found myself wandering the woods...</i>

16:07.490 --> 16:11.240
<i>I found a massive tree 
that was bathing in sunlight,</i>

16:11.240 --> 16:13.970
<i>which ended up causing a slight problem.</i>

16:15.520 --> 16:19.630
<i>There's a race of creatures 
called dryads in this world.</i>

16:20.000 --> 16:23.880
<i>According to Gobji, they seduce 
males of intelligent races,</i>

16:23.880 --> 16:26.460
<i>and prey on them for nutrients.</i>

16:26.990 --> 16:29.620
<i>There are only female dryads,</i>

16:29.620 --> 16:32.770
<i>and they're all supposed to 
be exceptionally beautiful,</i>

16:32.770 --> 16:35.970
<i>with no shortage of men 
falling prey to their wiles.</i>

16:35.970 --> 16:39.090
I wouldn't wanna run into them 
unless I was going to die anyway!

16:39.090 --> 16:40.470
Don't look so excited about it!

16:40.890 --> 16:44.980
<i>As for why I'm remembering this right now...</i>

16:48.120 --> 16:50.840
What huge muscles!

16:48.120 --> 16:53.490
<i>One of those dryads is right in front of me.</i>

16:50.840 --> 16:53.490
It's like I can feel how strong you are.

16:54.370 --> 16:58.500
I won't do anything, 
but could we at least talk?

16:58.500 --> 17:02.520
<i>Every glance, every breath, 
every bead of sweat...</i>

17:02.520 --> 17:05.500
<i>seemed to be laced with a charm effect.</i>

17:05.500 --> 17:07.660
So big!

17:06.210 --> 17:08.900
<i>And any reactions I had were only natural!</i>

17:08.900 --> 17:12.460
<i>Even if I hadn't been in a past life, 
I was a virgin this time around!</i>

17:12.460 --> 17:13.510
What do you want from me?!

17:15.120 --> 17:18.210
<i>If I don't do something soon, 
I'm going to be turned into food!</i>

17:18.210 --> 17:21.020
<i>And I would rather avoid that! Which is why...</i>

17:21.020 --> 17:25.270
<i>It's time to break out an 
ability I've never used before!</i>

17:26.520 --> 17:27.020
[Libido]

17:30.750 --> 17:33.420
O-Oh, wow!

17:33.800 --> 17:35.280
Miss Dryad...

17:37.740 --> 17:39.210
It's time.

17:40.600 --> 17:43.860
Wow, you're pretty rough, huh?

17:44.170 --> 17:45.590
But that's okay.

17:46.430 --> 17:54.630
<i>For five hours, we indulged our carnal hungers, 
like devouring the rarest of steaks.</i>

17:59.640 --> 18:01.640
<b>Gobrou obtained [Mistletoe's Felicitation]!</b>

18:02.870 --> 18:04.850
That was fantastic!

18:05.340 --> 18:06.910
Come see me again, okay?

18:06.910 --> 18:08.470
Maybe some other time.

18:08.470 --> 18:10.210
I'll be waiting.

18:11.000 --> 18:13.570
<i>I'm not going to get into 
a lot of specifics, but...</i>

18:14.030 --> 18:15.530
<i>That was awesome!</i>

18:16.690 --> 18:20.540
<i>After a short walk, I came across 
a lake with a waterfall.</i>

18:20.540 --> 18:24.040
<i>And while washing off 
the sweat and... other things...</i>

18:24.530 --> 18:27.040
<i>I found myself surrounded by lizardmen.</i>

18:29.630 --> 18:31.330
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Aquatic Life]</b>

18:29.630 --> 18:32.790
<i>Aquatic Life. Lizardman Language.</i>

18:31.330 --> 18:32.790
<b>You Have Learned the Ability [Lizardman Language]</b>

18:34.800 --> 18:38.820
Silver Arm Specialty: Jolt Counter!

18:39.090 --> 18:41.260
<i>I was absolutely invincible today.</i>

18:41.760 --> 18:46.770
<b>Day 42</b>

18:42.990 --> 18:46.770
<i>The next day, we found out that two goblins 
were capable of becoming mages.</i>

18:46.770 --> 18:50.280
<i>They were transferred to
 Hobsei's team immediately.</i>

18:51.550 --> 18:54.120
I'm so glad to finally have some students!

18:54.120 --> 18:56.850
I'm going to make sure they 
learn everything they need.

18:56.850 --> 19:00.280
<i>Is there some reason her 
smile is giving me chills?</i>

19:00.280 --> 19:04.780
<b>[Enchanting]</b>

19:01.230 --> 19:04.790
<i>Enchanting. The ability to give 
magic properties to matter.</i>

19:05.500 --> 19:08.440
<i>I tried it out with the smith, when...</i>

19:09.720 --> 19:11.760
You don't seem happy.

19:11.760 --> 19:12.800
It's fine.

19:13.290 --> 19:15.800
<b>Day 43</b>

19:14.040 --> 19:15.800
Hey, good morning!

19:19.220 --> 19:21.540
<i>Gobmi's in a foul mood.</i>

19:22.810 --> 19:26.070
<i>I didn't know why, so I asked around.</i>

19:26.440 --> 19:28.690
Sorry. Don't know.

19:28.690 --> 19:30.940
You oughta give it a good think.

19:30.940 --> 19:33.090
Think about it for a while.

19:33.710 --> 19:35.440
Ah, to be young!

19:40.600 --> 19:43.200
<i>As for the chef sisters...</i>

19:43.200 --> 19:45.250
Oh, perfect timing.

19:45.250 --> 19:47.400
We've got some new recipes for you to try!

19:47.400 --> 19:48.700
Those are poisoned.

19:49.180 --> 19:52.210
And so, you came to me.

19:52.830 --> 19:57.300
For someone who's generally pretty 
considerate, you can be surprisingly dense.

19:57.640 --> 20:00.240
I dunno what to say to that.

20:00.570 --> 20:02.720
To get straight to it...

20:03.120 --> 20:06.220
They're jealous.

20:07.440 --> 20:10.730
Of the fact that you had an
 encounter outside of the village.

20:12.450 --> 20:14.830
You really didn't notice, huh?

20:14.830 --> 20:17.600
You've got a few hickeys on your neck.

20:19.410 --> 20:22.610
<i>That dryad is a scary girl!</i>

20:22.990 --> 20:26.870
<i>Well, that solves the mystery! 
But what do I do next?!</i>

20:26.870 --> 20:30.790
I can understand how they feel, too.

20:37.370 --> 20:39.000
<i>Huh?!</i>

20:40.330 --> 20:44.940
This is how I feel. What do you say?

20:45.750 --> 20:49.460
<i>I had no idea she was going to 
do something like this.</i>

20:49.460 --> 20:51.770
<i>Is she trying to get my favor?</i>

20:52.180 --> 20:58.030
<i>But... I can't deny I'm pretty pleased by this, 
and it's easy to get carried away...</i>

21:00.300 --> 21:02.700
That's bold of you.

21:02.700 --> 21:05.780
But I'm afraid I can't let it happen!

21:08.690 --> 21:12.540
Not... without me.

21:17.020 --> 21:19.520
Hey, don't try to leave us out!

21:19.520 --> 21:21.580
That's right! We all...

21:21.580 --> 21:24.050
...are thinking the same thing!

21:24.050 --> 21:29.060
I-I-If it's not too much trouble, 
could we also...

21:32.720 --> 21:36.060
<i>I'm not going to elaborate 
on what happened next.</i>

21:36.060 --> 21:43.070
<b>[Golden Thread]

[Aero Master]

[Metamorphose]

[Manipulating
Self-Body Fluid
Properties]</b>

21:36.060 --> 21:43.070
<b>[Libido]

[Vamp Up]

[Triple Thrust]

[Sneak Endurance]</b>

21:45.570 --> 21:53.080
<b>Creating a temporary private room with threads. [Aero Master] to provide soundproofing.</b>

21:46.690 --> 21:49.730
Don't even, Kichi. He's busy.

21:49.730 --> 21:53.080
<i>It was an incredibly pleasurable... 
and passionate night.</i>

21:55.790 --> 22:00.010
<i>And if anything happens... 
I'll take responsibility!</i>

23:30.010 --> 23:41.170
<b>Next time:</b>
